ok(P+"2022 Paper 1 Q16",r"Each round, $X-Y$ changes by $+5,0,-5$ with probabilities $\frac5{12},\frac16,\frac5{12}$. $P(X_2>Y_2)=(\frac5{12})^2+2\cdot\frac5{12}\cdot\frac16=\frac{45}{144}=\frac5{16}$, so $P(X_2\ge Y_2)=1-\frac5{16}=\frac{11}{16}$ by symmetry. $P(X_3=Y_3)=(\frac16)^3+6\cdot\frac{25}{144}\cdot\frac16=\frac{77}{432}$, and $P(X_3>Y_3)=\frac12(1-\frac{77}{432})=\frac{355}{864}$. So I-Q, II-R, III-T, IV-S.")
