ok(P+"2023 Paper 1 Q23",r"Adiabatic: $T_AV_0^{\gamma-1}=T_f(5V_0)^{\gamma-1}$, so $T_A=5^{\gamma-1}T_f$. Isothermal: $T_B=T_f$. Hence $T_A/T_B=5^{\gamma-1}$. Note that $T_A>T_f$, since adiabatic expansion cools the gas.")
ok(P+"2023 Paper 1 Q24",r"$g\propto\frac1{(R+h)^2}$, so $\frac{g_P}{g_Q}=\frac{(R+h_Q)^2}{(4R/3)^2}=\frac{36}{25}$. This gives $R+h_Q=\frac65\cdot\frac{4R}{3}=\frac{8R}{5}$, so $h_Q=\frac{3R}{5}$.")
