fix(P+"2023 Paper 1 Q51",r"Benzene with $\mathrm{CH_3Cl/AlCl_3}$ gives toluene, the Etard substrate (P-3). Aniline with $\mathrm{NaNO_2/HCl}$ gives a diazonium salt, the Gattermann substrate (Q-4). Phenol with Zn dust gives benzene, the Gattermann-Koch substrate (R-5). Toluene with $\mathrm{KMnO_4}$ then $\mathrm{SOCl_2}$ gives benzoyl chloride, the Rosenmund substrate (S-2). Trap: Clemmensen reduction of acetophenone gives ethylbenzene, which matches none of these.")
ok(P+"2023 Paper 2 Q1",r"Differentiate: $3f=f+xf'-x^2$, so $xf'-2f=x^2$, i.e. $\left(\frac f{x^2}\right)'=\frac1x$. Hence $\frac f{x^2}=\ln x+c$, and $f(1)=\frac13$ gives $c=\frac13$. So $f(e)=e^2\left(1+\frac13\right)=\frac{4e^2}{3}$.")
ok(P+"2023 Paper 2 Q2",r"Let $p=\frac13$, $q=\frac23$, and let $a$ be the probability of finishing with heads given the last toss was H. Then $a=p+q\cdot pa$, so $a=\frac p{1-pq}=\frac37$. Starting fresh, $P=pa+q(pa)=pa(1+q)=\frac13\cdot\frac37\cdot\frac53=\frac5{21}$. Trap: answering $p^2/(p^2+q^2)$ ignores the alternating structure.")
ok(P+"2023 Paper 2 Q3",r"Let $u=\frac{6y}{9-y^2}$. For $0<y<3$, $u>0$ and $\cot^{-1}(1/u)=\tan^{-1}u$, so $\tan^{-1}u=\pi/3$. Then $y^2+2\sqrt3y-9=0$ gives $y=\sqrt3$. For $-3<y<0$, $u<0$ and $\cot^{-1}(1/u)=\pi+\tan^{-1}u$, so $\tan^{-1}u=-\pi/6$. Then $y^2-6\sqrt3y-9=0$ gives $y=3\sqrt3-6$. Sum $=4\sqrt3-6$. Trap: missing the $\pi$ shift for negative arguments.")
ok(P+"2023 Paper 2 Q4",r"$\frac{\vec b+2\vec d}{3}=\left(\frac73,\frac83,\frac53\right)$, and $\frac{5\vec c+4\vec a}{9}=\frac{(17+4,16+8,35-20)}{9}=\left(\frac73,\frac83,\frac53\right)$. They match, so the point divides $PR$ internally in ratio $5:4$. It also lies on $QS$, so the four points are coplanar, and $|\vec b\times\vec d|^2=9^2+3^2+(-9)^2=171\ne95$.")
ok(P+"2023 Paper 2 Q19",r"$[Y]=ML^{-1}T^{-2}$, $[c]=LT^{-1}$, $[h]=ML^2T^{-1}$, $[G]=M^{-1}L^3T^{-2}$. Matching powers: M: $\beta-\gamma=1$; L: $\alpha+2\beta+3\gamma=-1$; T: $-\alpha-\beta-2\gamma=-2$. Solving gives $\alpha=7$, $\beta=-1$, $\gamma=-2$.")
ok(P+"2023 Paper 2 Q20",r"$a_x=\frac{dv_x}{dt}=\alpha\dot y=\alpha\cdot2\alpha x=2\alpha^2x$ and $a_y=2\alpha\dot x=2\alpha\cdot\alpha y=2\alpha^2y$. So $\vec F=m\vec a=2m\alpha^2(x\hat x+y\hat y)$. Trap: $\vec v$ is a velocity field, so differentiate along the motion; do not multiply $\vec v$ by $\alpha$.")
ok(P+"2023 Paper 2 Q21",r"$\gamma=1+\frac2n$ and $v=\sqrt{\gamma RT/M}$. At fixed $T$, fewer degrees of freedom means larger $\gamma$ and faster sound, so $v_5>v_7$. $U_n=\frac n2RT$ grows with $n$, so $U_5<U_7$. Option C satisfies both conditions.")
